        "id": 11059
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-11-09T14:10:33Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "`kFloatConstant` is referenced here:\n\n`const float kFloatConstantAlias \u003d kFloatConstant;`\n\n`kFloatConstant` is not replaced with the literal value `2.14` because the variable is not part of a larger expression. Variables in isolation don\u0027t constant-propagate. As soon as it participates in a larger expression, folding will kick in.\n\n(VariableReferences in isolation do not constant-propagate because we expect every driver to be smart enough to emit good code for `const float PI` without our help. That\u0027s table stakes, right? It\u0027s not an optimization unless there\u0027s some sort of benefit in the final results; otherwise, it\u0027s just wasted work.)\n\nIf we use both IsCompileTimeConstant or GetConstantValueForVariable when deciding to emit OpVariable or not, I _believe_ we will avoid emitting an OpVariable here, because we will see that `kFloatConstantAlias` has a compile-time-constant value after variable-to-value substitution and the SPIR-V code-gen will handle the rest. I don\u0027t expect the decl to disappear in other backends and that\u0027s OK; I trust the drivers to do their part.",
      "parentUuid": "5359b490_f96aded8",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 7,
        "startChar": 21,
        "endLine": 7,
        "endChar": 35
